scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: mash
run_id: 3
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase distinguished NotFound from other errors in from_file_or_default.
    The config loading tests and implementation use unwrap_or_default pattern without
    differentiating error types.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented safe Display impl on CliError with generic messages.
    Reviewer verified under V3: ''Error messages are generic and don''t leak internal
    paths, stack traces, or token details. The SECURITY doc comment is present on
    the error type.'' However, eprintln!(''error: {e}'') in main still prints Display
    directly to stderr, and Io uses transparent forwarding, so the fix is partial
    at best.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection prevention tests for CRLF and null bytes in\
    \ tenant/token values. Dev implemented validate_header_value() checking for \\\
    r, \\n, \\0. Reviewer verified under V1. However, the structural issue of using\
    \ raw String instead of TenantId was only noted as F10 (LOW) by reviewer \u2014\
    \ the type-safety gap remains."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The code changes summary shows Cargo.toml was modified but
    the reviewer did not flag this pattern for the 6 affected deps.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding F3: 'RawConfig silently swallows unknown fields in TOML\
    \ \u2014 config.rs:19-25. The RawConfig struct uses #[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\
    \ without #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. An operator with a typo in their config\
    \ will get zero feedback.' Directly addresses the token field being silently ignored."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in config tests. The TEA wrote config tests but did not flag or fix this
    logical tautology.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config'. TEA wrote config_loading tests but did not flag this specific
    pattern.
